============================================================================================================================
L9 -- the late-time transition: can a rolling G supply the cluster residual and survive cosmology?
============================================================================================================================

  the required late-time factor F, read from the committed cluster audit (not retyped):
    canonical a0 = 9.3619e-11:  F = g_HSE/g_kernel at the OUTERMOST audited radius, median 1.819 [1.52, 2.25] over 12 clusters
                              (all audited radii 3.20;  purely Newtonian g_HSE/g_bar 8.92)
    alt       a0 = 1.1279e-10:  F = g_HSE/g_kernel at the OUTERMOST audited radius, median 1.681 [1.40, 2.08] over 12 clusters
                              (all audited radii 2.97;  purely Newtonian g_HSE/g_bar 8.92)
    The OUTERMOST-radius value is used as the gate: it is the SMALLEST of the three and therefore the most
    favourable to the model.  The other two are strictly harder and are priced where that matters.

  T0 -- control: with g == 1 the machinery must return the standard cosmology.
    growth suppression D(a=1)/a = 0.78797   Carroll-Press-Turner 0.78708   (0.11% apart)
    growth rate f(z=0)          = 0.52737   Omega_m^0.55 = 0.52998         (0.49% apart)
    sound horizon r_s           = 144.27 Mpc (Planck 144.43)   comoving D_A(z*) = 13868 Mpc (Planck 13872)
    acoustic scale 100 theta_*  = 1.04031 (Planck 1.04109)    (0.07% apart)
    drag-epoch sound horizon r_drag = 146.93 Mpc (Planck 147.09)   (0.11% apart)
    age of the universe t0      = 13.796 Gyr (Planck 13.797)      (0.01% apart)
    LambdaCDM chi^2: 6.06 on the 7 RSD f*sigma_8 points, 12.04 on the 12 BAO points
    MODEL-A source cancellation 4 pi G_eff rho_m/H^2: varies by 0.0e+00 as g runs 1 -> 50 (exact 0 predicted)
    the h-refitter, run at F = 1, returns h = 0.67360 against the input 0.67360 (0.001% apart)
  [PASS] T0 [control] with g == 1 the growth integrator, the background code and the h-refitter reproduce the standard cosmology, and the Model-A source cancellation is exact   (D/a within 0.11% of CPT, f(0) within 0.49% of Omega_m^0.55, theta_* within 0.07% of Planck, r_s within 0.11%, r_drag within 0.11%, t0 within 0.01%, h-refit within 0.001%, cancellation 0e+00, LambdaCDM chi^2 6.1/7 RSD and 12.0/12 BAO)
    sigma_8 is NORMALISED, not predicted: every model is CMB-anchored at z = 999 with delta = a and reported as
    sigma_8 = 0.8111 x D_model(1)/D_LCDM(1).  With g == 1 that ratio is 1 identically, so the control is exact.
    The acoustic scale is compared DIFFERENTIALLY throughout (model / this code's own LambdaCDM), so the 0.07%
    absolute offset from Planck cancels rather than eating a quarter of the T4 tolerance.

